    "description": "Siri Engineer for Korean 2011- present\n\nResponsible for developing natural language processing for the Korean Siri.  As a native Korean speaker, I am able to discern the details of the Korean language.  This helps me to assist Korean Siri to understand more natural spoken inputs from the user. \n\nAs assistant evolved over the years, I helped with Siri transition into the ML. Working to harness the power of AI in assistant. \n\nLocalizability Project Engineer 2000 - 2011\nResponsible for releasing Localization ready software for all Apple Software that got released to the world-wide. Responsibilities also covered Windows based software releases like iTunes and  QuickTime. With extensive internationalization experience, I reported issues in the software that would hinder the functionality or UI of the international languages. Managed between engineering and the localization house to release projects on time with no serious localizability issues. \n\nInternational QA 1996 - 1999\nResponsible for Korean markets top 10 software compatibility for Mac OS. Acquired Internationalization knowledges though interaction with engineering team.\n\nLanguage Kit Engineer 1995 - 1996\nBased on the Mac OS 7, 8 and 9, Apple released Language Kits for various languages.  These were the patches that would go into English Mac OS and enable the users to read and write the language packs they install.  Responsible for the release of Japanese, Chinese, Korean, Arabic language Kits. \n\n\n\n",
